# Quirion Ranger: "Return a Forest you control to its owner's hand: Untap target creature. Activate only once each turn."
# Breeding Pool (a Forest Island, not named Forest) pays the cost on T5 to untap Bot2's tapped Llanowar Elves (any creature,
# an opponent's too; Bot2's Forest, not a creature, cannot be the target); a second activation the same turn is refused though a Forest is still there (Bot2's Forest does not
# count either). On T7 it works again, the Forest returned untapping Bot1's own tapped Elves. CR 602.5b, 118.3, 205.3i.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Quirion Ranger
Breeding Pool
Llanowar Elves
Island
Island
Island
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Quirion Ranger.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Breeding Pool.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Activate
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
? Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Tapped = true
! Bot1.Battlefield.Quirion Ranger.Activate(Bot2.Battlefield.Forest)
Bot1.Battlefield.Quirion Ranger.Activate(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Choose(Breeding Pool)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Tapped = false
? Bot1.Battlefield.Breeding Pool = (absent)
! Bot1.Battlefield.Quirion Ranger.Activate
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Activate
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Quirion Ranger.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Choose(Forest)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Llanowar Elves; Quirion Ranger
